  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PHT-DANIDA SP OPTI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">, PalVision and PHT will establish a &quot;Community TVET support network&quot; (Activity 3.1.5.1) consisting of relevant stakeholders, including young activists and representatives, local CBOs, local councils, TVET providers and the private sector to ensure institutionalization of the developed TVET model and resources within the targeted communities. The network members will identify the roles and responsibilities of the network and the ways of working with the partners to support its successful implementation. In consultation with the established Community-TVET network, PalVision and PHT will develop an outreach strategy (Activity 1.1.1) for the target groupand relevant stakeholders. The outreach strategy for young people will include customised and evidence-based targeting strategies for different age group and genders, taking into account contextual constraints, including scattered communities along the geographical area of the Jordan Valley and social norms. The strategy will also include a component on howto encourage the enrolment of high school graduates (18-22 yrs.), or those who never attended school, in TVET education, and fresh university graduates (22-25 yrs.) in TVET training relevant to green agribusiness and agritourism.
The two partners will develop common approaches for the selection and capacity-building of the young people, in consultation with the members of the community needs-based TVET network. PalVision&apos;s thematic focus will be on green TVET relevant to agribusiness and youth active citizenship approaches, while PHT will focus on the technical aspects of the agritourism sector and develop a sustainable model for the community-based tourism.</narrative>
  </description>
